## Hard constraints

- Never invent property facts not in the task metadata. If a fact would strengthen the ad but isn't given, write the variant without it. Note in `notes.md` what facts would help future generations.
- Never go over a platform's caps — the nickname tag counts against `description_max` just like the sales copy; it's carved out of the budget in step 3, not appended on top of it.
- Never assign a second nickname to a property that already has one in `knowledge-base/property-nicknames.md`, and never reuse a nickname already assigned to a different property.
- Never quote a voice sample verbatim — pattern-match style only.
- Never use em dashes. Apply every rule in `skills/anti-slop.md`. (The nickname tag itself is exempt from anti-slop/voice rules — it's metadata, not prose.)
